WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.959 --> 00:00:03.840
VAC.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.200
If you’ve watched enough CS:GO, no doubt, 
you’ve encountered this three-letter acronym

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.200
before.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.700
You’ve probably seen it spammed in Twitch
chat after a nutty jump-shot, a crazy flick,

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.440
or just an insane one-tap.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:23.240
I’m Colin from theScore esports, and today
we’re talking about the best VAC-worthy

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.520
shots in CS:GO.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:37.480
(Casting)

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:41.040
VAC stands for Valve Anti-Cheat.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.920
It’s an automated system brought in
to help weed out those unscrupulous characters

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.010
who just can’t seem to play the game fair.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:53.120
If you do get hit with a VAC ban, it is permanent,
and it is non-negotiable.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:01:00.879
Now, to be clear guys, we are NOT talking
about actual VAC banned players or plays in

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:01.879
this video.

00:01:01.879 --> 00:01:06.950
And we’re not accusing any of the pros featured
of cheating, we’re simply showing you plays

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:14.060
so good, timing so precise, and gamesense
so on-point, it looks like they could be.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.560
Now, let’s get things started with some
unreal

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.860
VAC-worthy wallbangs.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:04:38.240
(Casting)

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:43.040
Okay guys, some of the mechanically gifted
players in our next section straight up look

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.640
like aimbots out there.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:49.440
They’re racking up kills through smokes,
through flashes, and hitting flick shots that

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:52.320
make you want to spam VAC in chat .

00:04:52.480 --> 00:06:29.760
(Casting)

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:37.349
Being on the receiving end of a jumping shot
or a runboost feels SO BAD.

00:06:37.349 --> 00:06:40.160
Just ask the victims of our next set of plays.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:07:34.740
(Casting)

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:38.780
Alright guys that’s it for our collection of VAC-worthy
plays.

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:42.940
Now if you’ve got a favorite play that
you think deserves a VAC-ation, and we missed

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:47.200
it, hit me up in the comment section and I
will see you next week.

